BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//WebMS Intra//Test fixture//EN
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:What this proves: several skipped dates written on ONE line, separated by
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:commas. Microsoft 365 writes its skipped dates that way; Google writes one
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:EXDATE line each (exdate-multi-lines.ics covers that shape). A reader that
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:does not split on the commas treats the whole line as one unreadable date,
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:skips nothing, and quietly puts deleted dates back into a Microsoft calendar.
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:Five Tuesdays with the second and fourth removed leaves three.
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:exdate-one-line-1@fixtures.webms.test
DTSTAMP:20260901T090000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261006T190000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261006T200000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;COUNT=5
EXDATE;TZID=Europe/London:20261013T190000,20261027T190000
SUMMARY:Tuesday meeting
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
